# Wetar — BLoC & Project Structure

## 1. Feature-First Directory Layout

Code lives in `lib/features/<feature>/` using clean layer separation:

- **Feature Modules (strict canonical names):**
  `player`, `library`, `music_folders`, `playlists`, `equalizer`, `lyrics`, `personalization`, `settings`, `onboarding`

Within each feature:

| Layer | Directory | Contents |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Data** | `data/` | Repository implementations, Drift DAO queries, platform-channel adapters, isolate parsers |
| **Domain** | `domain/` | Pure Dart entities, repository interfaces, use-case/domain calculators (e.g., LRC parser, ReplayGain math, scan diffing) — **zero Flutter UI or platform imports** |
| **Presentation** | `presentation/bloc/` | `Bloc` / `Cubit` classes and `Equatable` immutable states |
| **Presentation** | `presentation/screens/` | Thin screen shells (`*_screen.dart`) composing routes, `BlocProvider`, and adaptive layouts |
| **Presentation** | `presentation/widgets/` | Scoped, reusable feature widgets |

Shared infrastructure lives in `lib/core/` (`database/`, `capabilities/`, `logging/`, `platform/`, `storage/`, `router/`, `utils/`, `widgets/`).

---

## 2. Single Source of Truth for Playback (`WetarAudioHandler`)

- **Hard Rule:** One singleton **`WetarAudioHandler`** (`audio_service` wrapping `just_audio` + `audio_session`) owns **all** audio playback state, queue state, audio focus, interruptions, sleep timer, A–B loop, ReplayGain attenuation, and state restoration persistence.
- **UI & BLoCs never talk to `just_audio` or `AudioPlayer` directly.**
- Widgets only dispatch semantic intents to `PlayerBloc` / `QueueCubit` (e.g., `PlayerPlayTrackRequested`, `PlayerSeekRequested`, `QueueReordered`), and `PlayerBloc` translates those into `WetarAudioHandler` actions and mirrors its streams into immutable UI state.
- Destroying or recreating the UI (configuration change, backgrounding, navigation, compact desktop toggle) must **never** interrupt or reset `WetarAudioHandler`.

---

## 3. Thin Screens & Zero Business Logic in UI

- `*_screen.dart` files handle layout composition, responsive phone/desktop adaptation, `BlocProvider` wiring, and `BlocListener` navigation/feedback triggers only.
- Extract sub-sections into small private or `presentation/widgets/` classes before any `build()` method grows complex.
- Widgets must never run SQL queries, `dart:io` file reads, tag parsing, color extraction, or sorting/filtering math inside `build()`.

---

## 4. State Ownership, Concurrency & Rebuild Scoping

- Every BLoC/Cubit state is immutable (`Equatable` + `copyWith`), explicitly modeling loading, ready, empty, recoverable error, and optimistic mutation states.
- Use `BlocSelector` and `buildWhen` everywhere lists, seekbars, or artwork update so a 250ms playback position tick **only** rebuilds the seekbar/time labels, never the full player screen or library grid.
- Deduplicate or cancel superseded async intents (e.g., search queries, folder rescans, palette extractions) so stale results never overwrite newer state.
- Register singletons and factories cleanly in `get_it` (`lib/core/di/service_locator.dart`), keeping platform-neutral domain/BLoC tests mockable without platform channels.
